{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I appears to interact with A2780cisR through a series of molecular targets that are all involved in sialylation pathways. The evidence suggests that Stecholide I acts as a modulator of a sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a key player in the synthesis of sialic acid residues on glycoproteins. This sialyltransferase is targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, and 5,8-Dihydroxy-2-(2-phenylethyl)chromone. These compounds are all known to influence the sialylation process, and their interaction with the sialyltransferase enzyme implies that Stecholide I may exert its effects by regulating the activity of this enzyme. The shared target of these compounds and the involvement of the sialyltransferase in the pathway suggest a potential mechanism by which Stecholide I influences A2780cisR, possibly through modulation of sialylation events. The evidence supports a role for Stecholide I in the regulation of sialyltransferase activity, which in turn may affect the function of A2780cisR.",
